1
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,040
I'm so hungry.

2
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,640
Sugar wheat cake.

3
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:51,560
Beef dumplings.

4
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:52,320
Dumplings.

5
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,120
I really want a bowl of
fragrant white rice.

6
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:02,800
Hurry up, or my mom will scold me.

7
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,319
My grandpa made roast goose today.

8
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:06,520
Let's meet under the tree after eating.

9
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,960
This family made winter melon soup

10
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,420
and steamed pork knuckle.

11
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:26,170
Too bad the steamed pork knuckle
is a bit lacking.

12
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:31,520
This is

13
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,440
spicy and savory.

14
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,120
There's beef tripe and duck blood.

15
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,120
They used...

16
00:01:43,479 --> 00:01:45,520
They used top-quality
Hanyuan Sichuan peppercorns

17
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,250
and Erjingtiao chili peppers.

18
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,720
Now for the crucial step.

19
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,960
Add chopped green onions,
white sesame seeds,

20
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,680
dried chilies, and Sichuan peppercorns.

21
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,539
Pour a spoonful of hot oil over it.

22
00:01:58,039 --> 00:01:59,200
Done.

23
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,730
It's spicy blood curd stew.

24
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,240
Besides the spicy blood curd stew,

25
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,840
we made other dishes at home.

26
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,800
A-choy, cucumber salad,

27
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,560
steamed pork with rice flour,
and dried shrimp soup.

28
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,360
Miss,

29
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,280
how is your nose so sharp?

30
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,400
Not only do you have a sharp nose,

31
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,860
but you're also so pretty.

32
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,240
Little boy,

33
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,960
you're such a sweet talker.

34
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,960
What's your name?

35
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,090
My name is Liang Yan.

36
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,680
You can call me Huohuo.

37
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:24,840
Huo Huo.

38
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,920
Do you want to come upstairs for dinner?

39
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,200
Can I?

40
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,200
Of course.

41
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:31,930
Let's go then. Let's go.

42
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,200
Have a seat.

43
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,460
Dinner will be ready soon.

44
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,120
I'll get you some tableware.

45
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,800
I brought my own.

46
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,120
I just need a spoon.

47
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,800
Shen Feng.

48
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,760
You're bringing strangers home now?

49
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:00,520
Brother.

50
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:03,120
This pretty lady is
a new friend I just made.

51
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,850
Sorry to intrude. I'll be leaving now.

52
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,160
My brother

53
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,400
is just like that.

54
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,740
He has a sharp tongue but a soft heart.

55
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,240
I'll pay for the meal.

56
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,079
Our family isn't so poor that

57
00:03:17,079 --> 00:03:18,610
we need to charge for a meal.

58
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,440
Let's eat.

59
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,130
You have such a good figure too.

60
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,600
Whose else have you seen?

61
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,440
No one's.

62
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,960
I don't look at things like that.

63
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,490
I'm not that kind of person.

64
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:47,600
Aren't you hot?

65
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,520
No.

66
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,680
Some people

67
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,079
eat with their eyes.

68
00:03:52,079 --> 00:03:53,640
I don't want to be treated as a dish.

69
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:55,960
Look at mine. I have them too.

70
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:58,240
Have some modesty. Eat up.

71
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,160
Here.

72
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,040
Thank you.

73
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,800
Based on my not-so-shallow

74
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,760
but not-so-deep

75
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,200
experience in Sichuan restaurants,

76
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,280
this Mao Xue Wang

77
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,280
is the best I've ever had

78
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:31,720
in the world.

79
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,200
My brother studied abroad before.

80
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,920
He's a great cook.

81
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:39,600
The young master
of our tea estate studied abroad?

82
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,460
Which country?

83
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,680
Sweden.

84
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,200
Sweden?

85
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,360
What a coincidence.

86
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:46,290
I wanted to go to Sweden before too.

87
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,000
But unfortunately, I couldn't make it

88
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
for some reasons.

89
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,960
If you could go to Sweden,

90
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,280
why did you stay here?

91
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,480
So what?

92
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,050
Who wants to be like you,

93
00:04:57,159 --> 00:04:58,720
working like a dog
for others in a big company

94
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,960
in a big city?

95
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,160
Why are your words

96
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,160
as pungent as Sichuan peppercorns?

97
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,200
How did I offend you?

98
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,360
You just did.

99
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:07,610
I don't like you.

100
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,560
You're not allowed
to eat these bean sprouts.

101
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,880
Zero people care, okay?

102
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,610
I don't even like bean sprouts.

103
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,480
Huo Huo, I want some duck blood.

104
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,400
This is ham.

105
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:24,960
Where

106
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,840
is your hometown?

107
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,200
What kind of guys do you like?

108
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:32,040
The cute and lively type,

109
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,380
or the devastatingly handsome type?

110
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,920
I'm the second son of the tea estate.

111
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,320
My brother is the eldest.

112
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,720
Not only does my family
own tea plantations,

113
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,120
but my brother also has his own tea brand.

114
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,730
How about you be my sister-in-law?

115
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,520
Does your brother know

116
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,980
you're out here
playing matchmaker for him?

117
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,200
But why is your surname Liang

118
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,400
and your brother's Shen?

119
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,680
He took our dad's surname.

120
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,840
I took our mom's.

121
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:00,240
A lot of people in our village do that.

122
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,800
Is this what they call

123
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:03,880
a two-sided marriage?

124
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:06,000
My parents are very much in love.

125
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,080
They're traveling right now.

126
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,160
It's just me and my brother at home.

127
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,640
Look,

128
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,480
isn't my brother pretty handsome?

129
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,400
Just give my brother a chance.

130
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:19,680
Your most important task right now

131
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,720
is getting into middle school,

132
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,200
not playing matchmaker.

133
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:23,920
Let's go.

134
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,680
Great mountains,
great water, great scenery.

135
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,940
Great smell, great craving, great food.

136
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,440
Who did you eat with today?

137
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,450
With a handsome guy.

138
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,480
Really? How handsome?

139
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:53,760
Do you like him?

140
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,080
Awesome!

141
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,120
He's very cute. I like him a lot.

142
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,240
Look, isn't he cute?

143
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,330
Sometimes I really hate how dense you are.

144
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,520
Yunbianshang is hiring.

145
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,680
Lawn event tomorrow morning.

146
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:23,410
Part-timer urgently needed.
Price negotiable.

147
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:30,560
Didn't they say

148
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,680
a part-timer was coming to help today?

149
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,880
Why isn't he here yet?

150
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,480
Are you okay?

151
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,560
It's you.

152
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,040
My friend works part-time here,

153
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,880
but something came up,
so I'm covering for him.

154
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,080
Such a small place,

155
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,120
yet you have connections everywhere.

156
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,050
I'll leave then.

157
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,880
Since you're already here,

158
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:57,960
just

159
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,159
help me out.

160
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:00,880
Thank you.

161
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,760
Ever since I inexplicably
came to this place,

162
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,520
I feel like

163
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,360
I'm playing a management game.

164
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,040
Working non-stop every day.

165
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,080
Then have you played Star Skeleton?

166
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:12,880
Of course

167
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,280
I haven't.

168
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,010
I've never even heard of it.

169
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,200
Think carefully before you speak.

170
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,730
I really haven't played it.

171
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,440
I've only played casual
mini-games like 4399

172
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,200
or Match-3.

173
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,040
What's wrong?

174
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,330
Are you a hardcore fan of this game?

175
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,640
I once met a girl in this game.

176
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:34,720
She pestered me every day
to help her rank up,

177
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:37,280
sweet-talked me,

178
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,280
and tricked me into
an online relationship.

179
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:40,360
But one day,

180
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,960
she deleted me for no reason.

181
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,080
I went looking for her,

182
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,480
only to find out
she already had a boyfriend.

183
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,440
See?

184
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,640
Online relationships aren't reliable.

185
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:50,170
They're all romance scams.

186
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,920
Good thing she only cheated on you

187
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,840
and didn't trick you into
going abroad for fraud.

188
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,440
It's a blessing in disguise.

189
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,330
Cheer up. Everything will be fine.

190
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:01,440
Hang in there!

191
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,360
Yeah,

192
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,520
a real blessing.

193
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:09,520
It's not like I'm the one who tricked you
into an online relationship.

194
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,680
Why are you so moody?

195
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,970
You can't run away
before the work is done.

196
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:28,480
What's wrong?

197
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,280
Qingqing, I have a favor to ask.

198
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:32,640
What is it?

199
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:37,200
I bombed my math test again.

200
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,000
If my brother finds out,

201
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,440
I'll get a spanking.

202
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,000
Qingqing,

203
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,520
could you forge a signature for me?

204
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:49,680
Huohuo,

205
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:52,450
how did you get a score
as low as your shoe size?

206
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,160
I just haven't figured it out yet.

207
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:57,480
But our family has genius genes.

208
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:58,320
Look.

209
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,200
Are these all your brother's?

210
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,120
Yeah.

211
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,600
Look at this.

212
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,120
This is the first Math Olympiad gold medal

213
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:09,160
my brother won at nine.

214
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:14,400
This is a photo of him with the president
of the International Mathematical Olympiad.

215
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,920
This row and the ones above

216
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,600
are all the gold medals
he swept for five years.

217
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,320
I'll be nine in three months.

218
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,480
Maybe by then,

219
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:24,400
I'll suddenly be able
to memorize the multiplication table.

220
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,440
Then I'll give you a medal too,

221
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,320
okay?

222
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,000
What's this?

223
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:39,400
This is my brother's most precious thing.

224
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,400
2847, I'll go buy a jigsaw puzzle.

225
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:45,120
Starting today,

226
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,360
I'll hide puzzle pieces

227
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:49,020
in every corner of the school.

228
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:49,880
You'll

229
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,240
follow my clues

230
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,920
and find the pieces one by one.

231
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,040
Once you find all the pieces
and complete the puzzle,

232
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,840
I'll give you a reward

233
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,250
and grant you a wish.

234
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,410
Dinner is ready.

235
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:08,100
Wash your hands first.

236
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,880
Let's go eat, sister.

237
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,580
Huo Huo, go wash your hands first.

238
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,000
I just remembered I have an emergency.

239
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,280
I won't eat here.

240
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,480
Trying to run away again?

241
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,600
I really have an emergency.

242
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,760
Besides, Yunbian is on the rise,

243
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:44,680
and I'm the acting manager.

244
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:45,760
I'm very busy.

245
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,520
I forgot to tell you.

246
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:57,960
My online date is called Yun Huhu.

247
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,160
You are 2847.

248
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,880
Yun Huhu,

249
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:18,040
I paid you to help me rank up,

250
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,320
not to drag me down.

251
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,680
Look how many times you fed this game.

252
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,320
You should change your name to Noob.

253
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,200
Boss, boss,

254
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:25,720
I didn't mean to.

255
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,080
Look at the enemy jungler.

256
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,760
I run into him every game,
and he hunts me down every time.

257
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,120
He's the top player on the server.

258
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,880
I can't beat him.

259
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,800
I don't want to play with you anymore.

260
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,480
Do you have the enemy jungler's
contact info?

261
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,880
Let's get him to carry us.

262
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,600
Who exactly is this guy?

263
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,600
How come I've never seen him before?

264
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,880
Even his name is system-generated.

265
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,720
You'd think he's a bot.

266
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:50,640
Let me see.

267
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,880
This is a real pro.

268
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,440
No doubt about it.

269
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,120
This 2847

270
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,520
is on the enemy team every time.

271
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:03,800
We played 20 games in total,

272
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:04,800
and he beat me 18 times.

273
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:07,120
Is it easy for me to earn
some milk tea money by boosting?

274
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,720
It's all ruined by this 2847.

275
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,960
Comrade Yun Huhu,

276
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,720
you need to change your mindset.

277
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,000
If you can't beat them,

278
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,080
join them.

279
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Master, I am enlightened.

280
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,840
Turn rivals into allies.
